    "id": "ncert.maths.ch03.ex3_2.q3iii.answer",
    "text": "Let x and y be the costs in rupees of one bat and one ball. Then 7x + 6y = 3800 and 3x + 5y = 1750. From the second, x = (1750 − 5y)/3. Substitution in the first gives 12250 − 35y + 18y = 11400, so y = 50 and x = 500. A bat costs ₹500 and a ball costs ₹50.",
