    "id": "ncert.maths.ch03.ex3_2.q3v.answer",
    "text": "Let x and y be the numerator and denominator. The conditions give (x + 2)/(y + 2) = 9/11 and (x + 3)/(y + 3) = 5/6, or 11x − 9y + 4 = 0 and 6x − 5y + 3 = 0. Solving gives x = 7 and y = 9, so the fraction is 7/9.",
