    "id": "ncert.maths.ch03.ex3_2.q3vi.answer",
    "text": "Let x and y be the present ages in years of Jacob and his son. The conditions give x + 5 = 3(y + 5) and x − 5 = 7(y − 5), or x − 3y − 10 = 0 and x − 7y + 30 = 0. Solving gives x = 40 and y = 10, so Jacob is 40 and his son is 10.",
